The dungeon is a list of -2, -3, 3, -5, -10, 1, 10, 30, and -5.
The rows is a list of 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, and 0.
The columns is a list of 2, 1, 0, 2, 1, 0, 2, 1, and 0.
The health is a list of 9 zeros.
For every step from 0 to 8.
The row is item step of rows.
The column is item step of columns.
The index is row times 3 plus column.
The need is 1000000.
If row is less than 2, set need to item (index plus 3) of health.
If column is less than 2 and item (index plus 1) of health is less than need, set need to item (index plus 1) of health.
If row is 2 and column is 2, set need to 1.
The here is need minus item index of dungeon.
If here is less than 1, set here to 1.
Set item index of health to here.

Show item 0 of health.
